# The working copy of this repo IS what the SFTP watcher uploads to production.
# Never let git rewrite line endings on checkout -- it would change the bytes
# served to browsers without any edit being made.
#
# `-text` alone was not enough: core.autocrlf was still `true`, so navbar.html and
# sidebar-manager.js had been checked out converted to CRLF while their blobs
# stayed LF, and git's stat cache reported the repo clean the whole time. autocrlf
# is now `false` locally in all three repos and the index was renormalized to the
# working bytes on 2026-09-16. Do not set autocrlf back to true here.
#
# Everything else in this repo is LF. `git status` being clean does not by itself
# prove the index matches the bytes on disk; `git hash-object <file>` against
# `git ls-files -s <file>` does.
* -text
